    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3c7a6733-a696-545c-9023-bb91084cc91d" activityNameId="aa1cd5c1-09a8-58ea-8d82-045e9a4cee38" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Anhydrite rock, at mine</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Anhydrite rock, at mine
The multi-output-process 'mining, gypsum' delivers the co-products 'gypsum, mineral, at mine' and 'anhydrite rock, at mine'. Allocation is done by weight. In some mines anhydrite is not exploited but left in the mine. Since the electricity consumption has a relevant share on the total energy consumption, the choice of the energy mix is important. For gypsum mined in countries with high fossil share in the electricity mix this module has to be adopted accordingly.;
CAS number: 013397-24-5; 
Formula: CaSO4 * 2 H2O; 
UUID: 9a74a6bb-85a2-3e1a-826c-6d86045589a4
mining and crushing of gypsum and anhydrite
Location: data for Switzerland
Technology: open pit mining; composition of products: 65% gypsum, 34% anhydrite, 1% others.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: environmental report, literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9a74a6bb-85a2-3e1a-826c-6d86045589a4.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
